# ── Site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
SITE_URL=https://questlaguna.org

# ── Payload CMS (all site content: announcements, slides, events) ──────
# BUILD-TIME env (content bakes into static pages). Leave unset to build with
# the built-in sample content (src/lib/sample-content.ts).
# CMS_TOKEN: the API key of a read-only "site" user in Payload. Because reads
# are authenticated, this key can also see drafts — which is what the preview
# route below needs.
# Note: changing either of these needs a REBUILD, not a restart — they are
# inlined at build time, including for the preview route.
CMS_URL=
CMS_TOKEN=

# Set to "true" IN PRODUCTION. Without it, an unreachable CMS or a wrong
# CMS_URL silently bakes in placeholder sample content and the build still
# succeeds. With it, that becomes a failed build instead.
# (It cannot catch a wrong CMS_TOKEN — Payload treats an invalid key as an
# anonymous reader, so published content still loads and only draft preview
# breaks. Test the preview URL after deploying.)
CMS_REQUIRED=

# ── Draft preview (RUNTIME env — set on the site service, not build) ────
# Enables the preview routes so editors can view an unpublished item live from
# the CMS before publishing:
#   /news/preview/<slug>?token=<PREVIEW_SECRET>
#   /events/preview/<slug>?token=<PREVIEW_SECRET>
#   /testimonies/preview/<slug>?token=<PREVIEW_SECRET>
# Unset = the routes are disabled and return 404. Use a long random value.
#
# Set the SAME value on the CMS service (cms/.env.example) — that is what puts
# the "Preview" button next to Save and builds these links. The site validates
# the token; the CMS generates it. A mismatch shows a button that 404s.
PREVIEW_SECRET=

# ── Prayer form email (RUNTIME env — set on the site service, not build) ─
# Unset = the form falls back to the Facebook Messenger handoff (no email).
# When all three are set, requests are emailed to the prayer team.
# RESEND_API_KEY: from resend.com (free tier). PRAYER_FROM_EMAIL must be a
# verified sender domain in Resend (e.g. prayer@questlaguna.org).
RESEND_API_KEY=
PRAYER_TEAM_EMAIL=
PRAYER_FROM_EMAIL=

# ── Question form email (RUNTIME env — set on the site service, not build) ─
# The Connect page "Ask a question" form. Unset = it falls back to the same
# Facebook Messenger handoff. When both are set (plus RESEND_API_KEY above),
# questions are emailed to the church admin/office inbox — NOT the prayer team.
# QUESTION_FROM_EMAIL must be a verified sender domain in Resend.
# This inbox also receives the /services enquiries. Those arrive with the topic
# "Pastoral services" and an "About: <service>" first line, so whoever reads it
# can forward to the right coordinator (PASTORAL_SERVICES in src/lib/site.ts).
QUESTION_TEAM_EMAIL=
QUESTION_FROM_EMAIL=

# NOTE: the CMS server's own env (database, admin, deploy hook, approver
# email) lives in cms/.env — see cms/.env.example and cms/WORKFLOW.md. It is
# never set on the site service.

# ── YouTube (BUILD-time — sermons archive) ─────────────────────────────
# Three tiers, best first:
#   1. KEY + the four playlist IDs → categorized archive with service tabs.
#   2. KEY only → real past LIVE broadcasts (filtered via liveStreamingDetails,
#      uncategorized).
#   3. Neither → keyless channel RSS feed (real recent uploads, uncategorized).
# Key from the Google Cloud console (enable YouTube Data API v3).
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_FAMILY=
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_YOUNGPRO=
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_YOUTH=
YOUTUBE_PLAYLIST_DAWN=
